# Build output. Note that Cargo.lock files ARE committed, including the one
# per excluded -capi package: pinning each shipped .so's dependency graph
# independently of the workspace is a deliberate release-engineering
# property of this architecture, not an accident (see "Workspace mechanics"
# in ARCHITECTURE.md).
/target/
crates/*/target/
crates/*/target-*/

# Generated language bindings (boltffi) — regenerate with `boltffi build`.
crates/*/dist/

# Built Python extension modules for the two deployment variants; produced
# by build-py.sh. The .pyi stubs and test battery beside them are sources.
py/v1/
py/v2/
# Free-threaded builds of the same two variants; produced by build-ft.sh.
py/ft/
py/ft2/

# Python virtualenvs, created on demand by build-py.sh / build-ft.sh.
/venv/
/venv-ft/

# Generated ABI dumps. Deliberately NOT committed: libabigail's XML bakes in
# absolute build paths and per-codegen-unit hashes, so the file is
# machine-specific and churns by ~300 lines on changes that abidiff itself
# correctly reports as no ABI change. Stripping that metadata to stop the
# churn makes abidiff silently stop detecting real breaks -- see
# "Full ABI diff" in ARCHITECTURE.md. The hand-written abi/*.abignore
# suppression files ARE sources and are committed.
abi/*.abi

# .NET build output; the .csproj and Program.cs are sources.
cstest/bin/
cstest/obj/

.DS_Store
